From: Calaos <https://github.com/calaos/calaos_base>
Subject: [PATCH] cpptui: allow the mandatory Ctrl+C interception to be disabled

Local patch carried by Calaos against the vendored copy of jonoton/cpp-tui
(upstream commit 9543ee3c056583eea1fc44491c6c240f0df0b570).

Why
---
App::run() treats Ctrl+C as a "Mandatory Global Exit": the event is caught at
the very top of the dispatch loop and sets running = false unconditionally,
before registered keys (register_key), before the focused widget and before
the exit keys ever see it. The single exception is when a widget currently
holds a text selection, in which case Ctrl+C means Copy and falls through.

That makes it impossible to write a TUI that must confirm before quitting:
calaos_config edits the Calaos configuration, and Ctrl+C on a screen with
unsaved changes has to open a "discard changes?" dialog rather than drop the
edits on the floor. No amount of registering or focusing can observe Ctrl+C
today.

What
----
Adds an opt-out on App, defaulting to the existing behaviour:

    void set_intercept_ctrl_c(bool intercept);   // default true
    bool intercepts_ctrl_c() const;

and guards the mandatory-exit branch with the flag. Upstream semantics are
byte-for-byte unchanged for anyone who does not call the setter. When the flag
is cleared, Ctrl+C simply continues down the normal dispatch path (contextual
copy, registered keys, focused widget, exit keys), so a register_key callback
or a focused widget can act on it. The Copy-on-selection special case is
untouched in both modes: with interception on it is the existing
handled_as_copy fall-through, with interception off the same contextual-copy
step and the widgets' own is_copy() handling run as usual.

Upstream status
---------------
Proposed upstream, see patches/UPSTREAM.md for the submission text. Drop this
patch as soon as an equivalent knob is released upstream.

Applying
--------
From the top of the calaos_base tree, against a pristine upstream header:

    patch -p1 < src/lib/cpptui/patches/0001-allow-ctrl-c-interception-to-be-disabled.patch
    # or
    git apply src/lib/cpptui/patches/0001-allow-ctrl-c-interception-to-be-disabled.patch
---
diff --git a/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp b/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp
--- a/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp
+++ b/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp
@@ -16196,16 +16196,26 @@ class App {
   }
 
   /// @brief Unregister a registered key combination
   void unregister_key(int key, bool ctrl = false, bool alt = false,
                       bool shift = false) {
     key_events_.erase({key, ctrl, alt, shift});
   }
 
+  /// @brief Enable or disable the mandatory global exit on Ctrl+C
+  /// @param intercept True (the default) to always exit on Ctrl+C, false to
+  /// dispatch Ctrl+C like any other key, so a registered key or the focused
+  /// widget can handle it (e.g. to confirm before discarding unsaved work).
+  /// The Copy-on-selection behavior of Ctrl+C is unaffected either way.
+  void set_intercept_ctrl_c(bool intercept) { intercept_ctrl_c_ = intercept; }
+
+  /// @brief Check whether Ctrl+C is intercepted as a mandatory global exit
+  bool intercepts_ctrl_c() const { return intercept_ctrl_c_; }
+
   // Dialog Stack
   std::vector<std::shared_ptr<Dialog>> dialog_stack;
 
   // Notification Overlay (for event dispatch)
   std::shared_ptr<Notification> active_notification_;
 
   /// @brief Register a notification widget for overlay event dispatch
   void set_notification(std::shared_ptr<Notification> notif) {
@@ -16515,17 +16525,17 @@ class App {
           last_resize_req = now;
           pending_resize_w = event.x;
           pending_resize_h = event.y;
           update_screen_size(event.x, event.y);
         }
 
         // 1. Mandatory Global Exit (Ctrl+C)
         bool is_ctrl_c = (event.is_key_event()) && event.is_copy();
-        if (is_ctrl_c) {
+        if (is_ctrl_c && intercept_ctrl_c_) {
           // Check if focused widget has selection - if so, let it consume the
           // event for Copy
           bool handled_as_copy = false;
 
           // Check active tooltip first
           if (active_tooltip_ &&
               active_tooltip_->selection_state_.has_selection()) {
             handled_as_copy = true;
@@ -16982,16 +16992,19 @@ class App {
   std::vector<std::function<void()>> posted_callbacks_;
 
   std::shared_ptr<Widget> focused_widget_;
 
   // Hover State
   std::shared_ptr<Widget> hovered_widget_;
   std::shared_ptr<Tooltip> active_tooltip_;
 
+  // Mandatory global exit on Ctrl+C, see set_intercept_ctrl_c()
+  bool intercept_ctrl_c_ = true;
+
   Buffer current_buffer_;
   Buffer previous_buffer_;
 
   void collect_focusables(std::shared_ptr<Widget> widget,
                           std::vector<std::shared_ptr<Widget>> &out) {
     if (!widget) return;
     // VISIBILITY CHECK: Skip hidden widgets and those with zero dimensions
     if (!widget->visible) return;
